WEBVTT

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.830
"Tokyo Performance Hall"

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.840
Thank you for coming all this way in the middle of a weekday.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.570
"Chinosuke Domon"

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.410
I'm glad there are so many people with nothing better to do.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.350
Tsutomu.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.890
What, you knew I was here?

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.860
Of course I did. Since you're here, you should have come see me.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.230
What? Heck, no. Too many people'd stare.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:36.130
They'd wonder what the young genius hit comedian's little brother is like.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:44.110
"Tokyo Performance Hall"

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.770
Would they?

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.870
Well, I've got things I need to do.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.110
Ah, Tsutomu, are you still doing that?

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.310
You know? Your internet...

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:51.080
Video uploads? Yeah, I am.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.600
"Setting Up

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.600
Please wait juuust a little longer."

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:55.750
You're really something special.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.750
You don't make any money from it,

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.220
"I ate boiled fish paste."

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:57.920
"A man who is one with his mount!

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:57.920
The ending that made all America cry!"

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.760
yet you're pursuing the essence of comedy for its own sake.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.250
"Warning, addictive viewing experience!

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.250
Endless laughter!"

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.420
"I tried becoming bait."

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.560
"I tried becoming bait.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.560
THE FINAL Into legend..."

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.420
"I hate seeing pricks like him

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.420
who've got it made screw around.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.420
I hope his videos die in a fire."

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.420
"Don't force us to watch

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.420
your boring shit you scrub."

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.220
I doubled over laughing again! Haruka.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:05.990
"Haruka: I doubled over laughing again!"

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.800
You're like a comedy bug.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.000
"Insect"

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.810
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:24.310
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:33.520
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:39.530
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.930
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:50.710
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:57.050
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.950
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.880
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.790
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:13.230
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:19.300
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:24.740
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:30.750
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.680
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.420
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.350
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.190
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:49.600
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.040
"Pierce It! The Insect Part"

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:01.910
Activating it should be possible, but Gattai is out of the question.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.750
This is a good opportunity to get some rest.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.180
For both the machine and you.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.890
A brief moment's respite for us, then, Savior-go.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.120
That name was rejected, you know.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.520
Commander, can I have a moment?

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:22.960
Pamyun! A hot young stud like
Hayato's asked me out for a drive!

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.260
Why go to the trouble of playing that character?

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.260
I wanted to speak with you. About Kaibuki.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:35.280
In the battle with the flame M.J.B.K. two weeks ago,

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.480
we would have been finished without him.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.780
You're right.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.480
It's true that Kaibuki does have high Verbalism Ability.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:49.220
But overreliance on a single person is a sign of an organization's weakness.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.250
"Flame"

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.590
At this rate, eventually...

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.290
...we'll fall apart?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.600
We... I couldn't do anything.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.470
We can't leave things as they are.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.400
That's a purrrty difficult conundrum.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.680
Don't push me. Don't push me.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.170
Huh?

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:17.180
Don't push me! Don't push me!

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.780
Agh! Someone push me--

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.660
M-Maia, you pushed him too hard.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.930
We're getting soup base out of Tsutomu!

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:34.460
Tsutomu Domon, this is the first
I've heard of you having a death wish.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.300
Hey, hey!

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.040
Drowning is prohibited on Shirobaco premises.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.010
That's our intimidating new waitress, Maia.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.880
Her natural sadism really gets me going.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.390
Sorry for the wait. Here is your
Bags Under the Eyes Latte.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.840
Mr. Customer, your eyes are all red!

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.700
Blech, they're eating it.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.400
Well, of course we are.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.700
Part hot oden, part boiling hot bath.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:09.660
I thought it'd be a real hit if it worked out.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:13.800
Want some?

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.650
This is... an in-in-indirect kiss?

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.550
With Akira.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:27.160
B-B-But, Tsutomu's broth, his juices are...

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.250
That's kind of...

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:34.100
Is that food with the hole in it good?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.530
What, you don't know <i>chikuwa</i>, either?

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.690
Want some?

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.330
No!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.750
I'm sorry. I didn't realize you liked it so much.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.390
Did you want to eat Akira's?

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:03.590
Y-Y-Y-You're wrong!

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.860
It hurts.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.230
I'm sorry!

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.790
"Subete Kenzaki"

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:17.610
I can't afford to rest here.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.900
I have things I have to do.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:26.080
Don't run away now, you hot young thing.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.480
You're the young heir to Nesta, aren't you?

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.590
Marrying into wealth is the best!

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:35.820
--Hurrah!
--S-Stop it!

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:38.060
They're like marriage hunting bugs.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.560
I'd better be careful, too.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.100
Let me go! Don't touch me!

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:46.120
I already have Maia! Spare me!

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.810
Hm? What is it?

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.510
I thought it would be rude to interrupt.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.780
Don't you have to go see him?

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:59.270
Not interested.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.650
You must have noticed when they launched last month.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:09.090
They've made changes to the OS on all the Vectors.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.360
That last battle was a risky one.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.460
Had the M.J.B.K. continued to devour his concept,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:21.170
the existence of Subete would have been wiped from this world.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:26.110
If that happened, would you have resented me for it forever?

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.980
If he were to be ended so easily,

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:32.000
that would mean he was never meant for anything greater.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.650
You're the same as ever.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.450
Do you feel that, Grandma?

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:42.190
It's like we're flying!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.960
What are you saying, Grandpa?

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.860
We're inside the bamboo grove.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.060
"Peachtanic"

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.030
That's when it happened!

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.530
A big peach floated along,

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.670
then collided with an iceberg and sank!

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.140
Cut!

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.480
Ah, something just feels off...

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.040
Shouldn't I be saving the peach?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.040
Hey!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.650
Let's see... Poisoned pineapple battle.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.320
Traveling around the world in a suitcase.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.190
Living for a week surrounded by shaved ice.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.550
What are all these?

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:16.560
The gags for the next video I'll upload.
Which sounded best?

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.830
You know, when I see your gags,

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:23.530
it's like you're trying to be novel, but aren't being novel in the least.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.500
You don't hesitate to just stab a guy where it hurts, huh?

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.770
How about, instead of reaction videos and sudden gags,

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:32.770
you do some more elaborate comedy?

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:35.610
Like <i>manzai</i> comedy, or storytelling.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.250
Not happening.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:43.580
Like anyone would get an elaborate joke these days.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.790
It's old-fashioned and lame.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.260
Um, Tsutomu?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.130
I'm using the modern medium of the internet

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:55.460
to find comedy that only I can perform.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:58.200
There's no point otherwise.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.760
Tsutomu Domon.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.470
Is what you're looking for... truly comedy?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.410
What is that?

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.650
"Tsutomu's Notes

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.650
Don't look. Don't look."

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.920
A book of gags?

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:21.260
Now, for a slightly odd news story.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:26.990
In Amanuma, Suginami-ku, a very healthy daikon is growing!

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.070
Not yet.

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.740
This isn't good enough to call the world's best tempura.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.140
Dear, what's gotten into you?

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.740
You haven't slept since yesterday.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:44.750
You've practically turned into a tempura-making bug.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.580
Don't push me!

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:50.340
"Aaa: How pathetic."

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:53.410
"Nanashi: Shitty video, die, die, die, die."

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.680
"tocoto: We don't want to see

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.680
a guy naked, you dumbass!"

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.990
Another amazing video!

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:01.830
"Haruka: Another amazing video!

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:01.830
Honestly, I doubled over laughing."

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.600
Honestly, I doubled over laughing.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:06.470
Hello, I'm commenting because
I happened to see your video.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:08.200
It was very funny!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.840
I don't think I've doubled over laughing like that before in my life!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.010
Some people may say unkind things about them, but I like your videos.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.650
They have me doubled over laughing every time.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:24.820
But sometimes I wish you'd do stories or one-man plays like you did at first.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:24.820
"Haruka: But sometimes I wish you'd do

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:24.820
stories or one-man plays like you did at first."

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.990
I like your reaction videos too, though.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:28.660
"Haruka: I like your

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:28.660
reaction videos too, though."

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:30.790
What's this? There's a bug here I've never seen before.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.290
It looks ugly. Maybe I ought to crush it.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:34.130
Huh? What's that?

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.560
Ma'am, how much is my bill?

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.200
Thanks for the food.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.070
Thank you.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.970
The Colic Bug, huh?

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.220
Rejoice.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.190
I shall now set you free.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.900
Mushi!

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.570
"Must Pass"

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.570
"Aim for Seisou U"

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.570
"Victory"

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:13.430
--Pass! Get my foot in the door!
--Study bug.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:13.430
"Study Bug"

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.070
Research... Research...

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:20.610
I must continue my research...
Must give everything to my research...

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.240
Research bug.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:22.080
"Research Bug"

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.510
Deava System, activate!

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.070
"Closed Today Due to Emergency"

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.590
The same thing again and again!
They never learn!

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.080
Don't let your guard down.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:40.900
Mushi.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.100
Gross.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:47.230
I thought so. It's an M.J.B.K. of the insect kanji.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.600
Size isn't everything!

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:50.910
Kujyo, Domon!

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:54.210
Confuse it with your speed and deal definite damage to it.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.980
Righto.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:59.110
--Sousei Gattai.
--Charge!

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.720
Jin!

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:04.720
"Jin"

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:10.560
They got eaten.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.660
Wh-Wh-Wh-What do we do?

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:16.130
Huh? The reading for Aquarion isn't vanishing.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.620
Could this be...

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.440
What's going on here?

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:26.770
Where is this place?

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:28.580
The frickin' bug's stomach?!

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.510
Oh, come on! Are you serious?!

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:39.820
"Voice ID

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:39.820
Shoko Iwagami"

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.610
...read me? Do you read me?

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:34.620
Shoko?

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.780
Tsutomu, are you okay?

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.250
I wonder if this counts as "okay"?

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.690
What do you think, Hayato?

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.090
Hayato?

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:48.000
Under the current government, economic recovery is a mere dream.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.460
--Now, we must raise the flag of reform
--H-Hayato?

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:53.130
with young and new powers!

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:56.640
In this current system, bound up by self-interested bureaucrats,

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:00.370
--can policies that are truly for the citizens be established?
--Hey, get it together!

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:01.840
This is bad!

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:06.680
By being inside it, they're suffering the effects of the M.J.B.K. directly!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:10.820
H-Hayato's dream is... to be a p-politician, so...

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:12.720
He's a politics bug, then?

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.390
Yes, the bureaucratic system

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.360
--Then Tsutomu is, too?
--circulates wealth smoothly,

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:19.730
--Tsutomu, are you okay?
--and it works to create an independent citizenry and bring happiness.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.060
Yeah, nothing's wrong with me.

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:24.530
However, with the difficult finances in this city...

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.230
Commander,

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:28.470
under the effect of this M.J.B.K.,

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:31.870
you lose sight of everything but your dreams and what you like.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.840
Like you've caught a bug that's made you obsessed with something.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.840
Yes, that's right.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.040
Well, I'll be fine, then.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:44.420
Because I... don't have something
I love, or a dream, or anything.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.420
But Tsutomu, you have comedy!

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:50.890
You're wrong. You're wrong...

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:55.850
I... I don't like comedy at all.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:04.210
My name is written with the characters for "work" and "insect."

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:06.110
"Tsutomu"

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.070
Lame, don't you think?

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:09.610
When I was little, I got laughed at for it all the time.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:12.610
But isn't it a laugh?

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:18.050
My parents gave me this name because they thought it was a good one.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:21.460
The Domon family have been <i>rakugo</i> comedians for generations, you know.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:25.860
We're a storied family that's produced masters for generations in a row.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:31.430
And my older brother,
Chinosuke, is a total genius.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.240
They've been calling him a prodigy since he was little.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:38.740
Since I was born into a family of comedians,

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:42.480
people expected the same from me, as the second son.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:46.280
But they thought that was cruel from the very beginning.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:50.890
So, to keep there from being a conflict in the first place,

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:54.990
Mom and Dad gave me a name I could never be a <i>rakugo</i> comedian with.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:58.630
My brother is Chinosuke. He is the land.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:01.560
And me, I'm an insect.

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:06.060
The little bug should crawl around on his giant brother's back, like bugs do.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:17.950
Screw that! Don't decide how I'll live for me!

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:20.510
Who gives a damn about traditional arts?!

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:22.850
It makes me sick!

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:25.790
I don't like it at all.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:30.290
I just wanted to smash it all.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:33.820
To break down tradition with my own comedy.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:37.830
Eggs?!

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.970
The M.J.B.K.'s babies will be born from them.

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:43.540
If we let them hatch, they'll likely start to eat words.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:47.800
If that happens, the word corrosion rate will...!

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.980
That was funny. I doubled over laughing.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.350
I loved it. I doubled over laughing.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:15:58.990
Don't tell me...

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:00.650
Tsutomu's so funny.

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:02.150
Haruka?

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.960
Tsutomu's fan?

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:08.060
She's a Tsutomu Domon bug, I guess.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.570
Can you hear it, Domon, this laughter?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.800
Even if you didn't like it yourself,

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:18.540
someone was this moved by and in love with your comedy.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:22.480
Don't you feel anything when you hear this voice?

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:24.040
I●●●

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:37.420
The truth is... I...

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:42.220
"Tsutomu's Notes

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:42.220
Don't look. Don't look."

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.730
That's Tsutomu Domon's...

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:47.390
"Rakugo plays to do:

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:47.390
- Manju are Scary

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:47.390
- Time Noodles"

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:51.670
A-Akira...?

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:54.680
As such, the youth who are concentrated in cities...

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.880
A lot goes on in life.

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.680
It's not bad to become engrossed in something.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.880
But if that's all you ever do, you'll tire of it.

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:07.590
And so, let me ask you

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:10.360
to hear this trivial story of mine.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:14.460
One morning when I woke up, a little bug crawled up to my pillow.

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:16.630
You're a dirty little thing.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:18.130
Maybe I'll crush you and throw you away.

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:21.470
And, when I lifted up my hand,
I heard this voice...

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.970
Please, don't!

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:24.740
Oh, the bug spoke.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.740
--Yes, my name is the colic bug.
--What is this?

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.940
--It's a pleasure to meet you.
--It's a <i>rakugo.</i>

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:34.250
Hey, the bug is really speaking!
Well, that's a surprise.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:37.750
Never seen that before.
And you're a colic bug, you say?

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:38.750
You must be a good bug.

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:44.430
I see! This M.J.B.K. is making itself grow by eating the kanji.

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:49.330
But if the kanji it's eating were to show a different meaning than usual...

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:54.800
If the bugs who are obsessed with things were to lose their focus...

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:58.310
It would affect the M.J.B.K. too, you mean?

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:01.000
We just need to make the bug kanji laugh!

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:05.680
B-B-But...

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:09.450
The bug's voice is too loud, so they can't hear.

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.820
That's no problem.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:14.950
For I am... the savior of comedy!

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:18.930
He suddenly told us to hook up loudspeakers to his Vector,

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:21.660
so we disconnected one of the base's big ones.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.200
What? The order didn't come from the commander?

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.470
Wait, a colic bug? You're a stomach illness!

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:30.500
You jerk. You've been making me suffer.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.000
I'll slay you!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:34.370
Please, don't do it!

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:38.480
If you'll spare me, I'll tell you our weakness.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:41.480
Your weakness? What's that? Speak up.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:45.120
You see, we really hate red peppers.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:48.990
When we're in a person's stomach, if they try to eat red pepper,

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:52.290
we flee lower and lower and take shelter in our other house.

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.990
Speaker, on!

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:56.000
Your other house?

00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:00.030
Yes, the one hanging between a man's legs.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.300
We flee to our other house there.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.510
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wha...?!

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:06.070
What's with this story?

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.640
The Colic Bug. It's a classic <i>rakugo</i> story.

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:10.640
Some house.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:13.650
Those are a man's important dangly bits!

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.520
The kanji are laughing!

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.390
--Tsutomu.
--Hayato?

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:21.410
What a silly story.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:26.360
Okay, fine, so you've got another dangly home to hide in on men.

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:28.400
What about when it's a woman?

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:31.530
You've got nowhere to run, then.

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:34.600
The Aquarion's being washed away in the bile.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:37.740
Ah! The bug is trying to expel them from its body!

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:41.040
In other words, the bug is deworming itself!

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:46.580
Here comes the punch line!

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.020
Let's do it, Hayato!

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:50.680
Sousei Gattai.

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:52.790
Pierce it!

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:57.950
--Aquarion!
--Aquarion!

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.260
--Ryu!
--Ryu!

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.300
"Ryu"

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:10.270
The kanji for insect originated as a variation of the one for dragon.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:15.380
If you laid eggs, that means you're female, right?

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:17.110
We have no other house in women.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:21.980
A woman's crotch is something you pierce through to create the future!

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:24.420
Tsutomu!

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:26.490
Pierce it!

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.460
Pierce it...!

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:32.790
Now, you shall be as a dragon who pierces the heavens!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:39.060
Pierce it!

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:42.960
"Pierce"

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:47.740
"Rainbow"

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.410
"Rainbow"

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:55.150
The dragon which broke through her crotch

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:57.450
rose to the heavens and became a rainbow!

00:20:57.450 --> 00:21:04.120
Mushi! Mushi! Mushi!

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:24.280
You know, at some point it became warped,

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:27.010
"Rakugo plays to do:

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:27.010
- Manju are Scary

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:27.010
- Time Noodles"

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:27.210
but I really did want to love comedy.

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:35.290
I wanted to learn to love it...

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:38.520
...but I didn't want to recognize that.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:44.400
But, from here on, I think
I'll try to face that fact.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:47.170
"There's something I really want

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:47.170
to tell you. Can we meet up?"

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:51.800
Haruka, you're the one who let me realize that. Let me thank you.

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:56.340
Man, my hands are so sweaty.

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:57.640
Are you Tsutomu?

00:21:57.640 --> 00:22:00.210
Yes!

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:03.020
My, you're quite the looker.

00:22:03.020 --> 00:22:07.520
Har... Ms. Haruka?

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:10.890
Yes, I am Haruka.

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.930
Oh, my.

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.400
That's all, folks.

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:51.690 --> 00:23:54.360
Maia, have you ever played hide and seek?

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:56.860
--What's that?
--Oh, I thought it might be the case, but...

00:23:56.860 --> 00:23:58.700
Maia, did you grow up shut away in a box?

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:00.830
Why would I need to be shut in a box?

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:03.140
Do you mean to imprison me again?!

00:24:03.140 --> 00:24:05.810
Worry not. I won't let anyone lock you away.

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:07.670
--For I am...
--Yes, yes, we know!

00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:09.210
Next time, Episode 9.

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:10.930
"Episode 9: Clear Them! The Inviting Shadows"

00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:10.880
"Clear Them! The Inviting Shadows."
